itial state:** User navigates to the home page. Multiple properties exist in the database.\n181-- **Expected:** Properties are displayed in a responsive grid: 1 column on mobile, 2 columns on tablet, 3-4 columns on desktop. Each property is rendered as a PropertyCard.\n182-\n183-#### Test: Property grid shows message when no properties match filters\n--\n...\n</persisted-output>"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f7a7c36-f6a4-4f04-ab3c-97ac5928ffeb","uuid":"7bd59026-c284-4121-8ed3-fdfbf893a879","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"7-### Component: AuthToggle\n8-\n9-#### Test: Auth page defaults to login mode\n10:- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/login` for the first time (not logged in).\n11-- **Expected:** The page displays in login mode with the email input field visible, a \"Log In\" submit button, and a toggle link reading \"Don't have an account? Register\" at the bottom.\n12-\n13-#### Test: Toggle from login to register mode\n--\n91-### Component: SearchBar\n92-\n93-#### Test: Search bar displays all input fields on load\n94:- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page (`/`).\n95-- **Expected:** The search bar is visible at the top of the page containing four inputs: a location text input with placeholder \"Where are you going?\", a check-in date picker, a check-out date picker, and a guest count selector. A search/submit button with a magnifying glass icon is visible.\n96-\n97-#### Test: Search by location filters property results\n--\n142-### Component: CategoryFilter\n143-\n144-#### Test: Category filter bar displays all property type chips\n145:- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page (`/`).\n146-- **Expected:** A horizontal scrollable bar of category chips is displayed below the search bar. Chips are shown for each property type: \"Apartment\", \"House\", \"Cabin\", \"Villa\", \"Condo\", \"Loft\", \"Cottage\", \"Townhouse\". No chip is selected by default (all properties are shown).\n147-\n148-#### Test: Clicking a category chip filters properties by that type\n--\n177-### Component: PropertyGrid\n178-\n179-#### Test: Property grid displays properties in a responsive grid layout\n180:- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page. Multiple properties exist in the database.\n181-- **Expected:** Properties are displayed in a responsive grid: 1 column on mobile, 2 columns on tablet, 3-4 columns on desktop. Each property is rendered as a PropertyCard.\n182-\n183-#### Test: Property grid shows message when no properties match filters\n--\n186-- **Expected:** The property grid area displays a \"No properties found\" message instead of an empty grid. The message suggests adjusting filters or search criteria.\n187-\n188-#### Test: Property grid loads and displays properties from API on initial page load\n189:- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page. Properties exist in the database.\n190-- **Expected:** The grid fetches properties via `GET /api/properties` and displays property cards. While loading, a loading indicator is shown. Once loaded, the property cards appear with correct data.\n191-\n192-### Component: PropertyCard\n--\n199-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. A property exists with at least one image (the first image by display_order).\n200-- **Expected:** The property card displays the main image (lowest display_order) at the top of the card with rounded top corners. If no image exists, a placeholder image is shown.\n201-\n202:#### Test: Clicking a property card navigates to property detail page\n203-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. A property with id \"abc-123\" is displayed.\n204-- **Action:** User clicks on the property card (not the favorite button).\n205:- **Expected:** The app navigates to `/properties/abc-123` (the property detail page).\n206-\n207-#### Test: Property card displays property type badge\n208-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties of different types exist.\n--\n228-- **Action:** User clicks the filled heart icon on the property card.\n229-- **Expected:** The app calls `DELETE /api/favorites/:propertyId`. The heart icon changes back to an outline (unfilled) style. The property is removed from the user's favorites.\n230-\n231:#### Test: Favorite button does not navigate to property detail page\n232-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page.\n233-- **Action:** User clicks the heart icon on a property card.\n234:- **Expected:** The favorite is toggled but the user remains on the home page. The click does not propagate to the card's navigation handler.\n235-\n236-#### Test: Favorite button is not shown when user is not logged in\n237-- **Initial state:** User is not logged in and is on the home page.\n238-- **Expected:** Property cards do not display the heart/favorite icon. Alternatively, clicking the heart redirects the user to the login page.\n239-\n240-#### Test: Favorite button reflects correct state on page load\n241:- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has previously favorited two properties. User navigates to the home page.\n242-- **Expected:** The app calls `GET /api/favorites` to fetch the user's favorites. The two favorited properties show filled/red hearts. All other properties show outline hearts.\n243-\n244-#### Test: Favorite button is functional on repeated use\n--\n249-### Component: FiltersPanel\n250-\n251-#### Test: Filters panel is hidden by default with a visible toggle button\n252:- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page (`/`).\n253-- **Expected:** The filters panel is collapsed/hidden. A \"Filters\" button (with a filter icon) is visible that the user can click to open the panel.\n254-\n255-#### Test: Clicking the Filters button opens the filters panel\n--\n331-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Previous\" button.\n332-- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show the first page of properties. The current page indicator highlights \"1\". The \"Previous\" button becomes disabled again.\n333-\n334:#### Test: Clicking a specific page number navigates to that page\n335-- **Initial state:** User is on page 1 of results. At least 3 pages of properties exist.\n336-- **Action:** User clicks page number \"3\".\n337-- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show the third page of properties. The current page indicator highlights \"3\".\n--\n352-#### Test: Pagination is functional on repeated use\n353-- **Initial state:** User is on page 1 of results with multiple pages available.\n354-- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\" (goes to page 2), then clicks \"Next\" again (page 3), then clicks \"Previous\" (back to page 2), then clicks page \"1\" (back to page 1).\n355:- **Expected:** Each navigation correctly updates the property grid and page indicator. The final state shows page 1 results.\n356-\n357-## Page: Property Detail (`/properties/:id`)\n358-\n--\n361-### Component: ImageGallery\n362-\n363-#### Test: Image gallery displays main large image and smaller thumbnails\n364:- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/properties/:id` for a property with 5 images.\n365-- **Expected:** The image gallery shows a grid layout with the first image (lowest display_order) displayed as a large main image, and the remaining images displayed as smaller thumbnails alongside or below it. All images have rounded corners.\n366-\n367-#### Test: Image gallery displays single image when property has only one image\n368:- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with exactly 1 image.\n369-- **Expected:** The single image is displayed as the main large image. No thumbnail grid is shown.\n370-\n371-#### Test: Image gallery displays placeholder when property has no images\n372:- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with no images.\n373-- **Expected:** A placeholder image or \"No images available\" message is displayed in the gallery area.\n374-\n375-#### Test: Clicking a thumbnail image makes it the main displayed image\n--\n383-- **Expected:** Each click updates the main image to the clicked thumbnail. The final state shows the first thumbnail as the main image.\n384-\n385-#### Test: Image gallery shows image captions when available\n386:- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page. The property has images with caption text set.\n387-- **Expected:** Captions are displayed below or overlaying their respective images.\n388-\n389-### Component: PropertyHeader\n390-\n391-#### Test: Property header displays title, location, rating summary, and host info\n392:- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/properties/:id` for a property with title \"Luxury Villa in Bali\", city \"Ubud\", country \"Indonesia\", an average rating of 4.7 from 23 reviews, hosted by \"Jane Host\" with an avatar.\n393-- **Expected:** The property header shows the title \"Luxury Villa in Bali\", location \"Ubud, Indonesia\", a star icon with \"4.7\" and \"(23 reviews)\", and the host name \"Jane Host\" with their avatar image.\n394-\n395-#### Test: Property header shows \"New\" when property has no reviews\n396:- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with no reviews.\n397-- **Expected:** The rating summary area shows \"New\" or no rating display instead of a numeric rating and review count.\n398-\n399:#### Test: Clicking review count scrolls to or navigates to reviews section\n400-- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page with reviews.\n401-- **Action:** User clicks the \"(23 reviews)\" link in the property header.\n402-- **Expected:** The page scrolls down to the ReviewsSection on the same page.\n--\n408-### Component: PropertyInfo\n409-\n410-#### Test: Property info section displays all property details\n411:- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/properties/:id` for a property with property_type \"Villa\", max_guests 6, bedrooms 3, beds 4, bathrooms 2.\n412-- **Expected:** The property info section displays: \"Villa\" as the property type, \"6 guests\", \"3 bedrooms\", \"4 beds\", and \"2 bathrooms\". Each detail has an appropriate icon.\n413-\n414-#### Test: Property info section displays check-in and check-out times\n415:- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with check_in_time \"15:00\" and check_out_time \"11:00\".\n416-- **Expected:** The property info section shows check-in time as \"3:00 PM\" (or \"15:00\") and check-out time as \"11:00 AM\" (or \"11:00\").\n417-\n418-#### Test: Property info section handles singular and plural labels correctly\n419:- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with max_guests 1, bedrooms 1, beds 1, bathrooms 1.\n420-- **Expected:** Labels display in singular form: \"1 guest\", \"1 bedroom\", \"1 bed\", \"1 bathroom\" (not \"1 guests\", etc.).\n421-\n422-### Component: PropertyDescription\n423-\n424-#### Test: Property description displays full description text\n425:- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/properties/:id` for a property with a multi-paragraph description.\n426-- **Expected:** The full property description text is displayed in a readable format with proper paragraph breaks.\n427-\n428-#### Test: Long description shows a \"Show more\" toggle\n429:- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with a very long description (multiple paragraphs).\n430-- **Expected:** The description is initially truncated after a reasonable length with a \"Show more\" link/button visible at the bottom.\n431-\n432-#### Test: Clicking \"Show more\" expands the full description\n--\n447-### Component: AmenitiesList\n448-\n449-#### Test: Amenities list displays amenities grouped by category with icons\n450:- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/properties/:id` for a property with amenities including \"WiFi\" (Essentials), \"Pool\" (Features), \"Smoke Detector\" (Safety), \"Near Beach\" (Location).\n451-- **Expected:** The amenities are displayed in groups with category headings: \"Essentials\", \"Features\", \"Safety\", \"Location\". Each amenity is shown with its icon and name.\n452-\n453-#### Test: Amenities list only shows categories that have amenities\n454:- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page. The property has amenities only in \"Essentials\" and \"Features\" categories (none in \"Safety\" or \"Location\").\n455-- **Expected:** Only the \"Essentials\" and \"Features\" category groups are displayed. Empty categories are not shown.\n456-\n457-#### Test: Amenities list shows \"Show all amenities\" when there are many amenities\n458:- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with more than 10 amenities.\n459-- **Expected:** An initial subset of amenities is displayed with a \"Show all X amenities\" button at the bottom (where X is the total count).\n460-\n461-#### Test: Clicking \"Show all amenities\" reveals the complete list\n--\n464-- **Expected:** All amenities are displayed, grouped by category. The button changes to \"Show less\" or disappears.\n465-\n466-#### Test: Amenities list displays message when property has no amenities\n467:- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with no amenities.\n468-- **Expected:** A message like \"No amenities listed\" is displayed, or the amenities section is not shown.\n469-\n470-### Component: BookingCard\n471-\n472-#### Test: Booking card displays price per night\n473:- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/properties/:id` for a property with price_per_night $150.\n474:- **Expected:** The booking card (sticky sidebar on desktop) shows \"$150 / night\" prominently at the top.\n475-\n476-#### Test: Booking card displays check-in and check-out date pickers\n477-- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page.\n--\n529-- **Action:** User interacts with the guest count selector.\n530-- **Expected:** The minimum selectable value is 1. The user cannot set guests to 0 or a negative number.\n531-\n532:#### Test: Reserve button shows error for unavailable dates\n533-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on a property detail page. The property has an existing confirmed booking for \"2026-05-01\" to \"2026-05-04\".\n534-- **Action:** User selects overlapping dates (e.g., check-in \"2026-05-02\", check-out \"2026-05-06\") and clicks \"Reserve\".\n535-- **Expected:** An error message is displayed (e.g., \"Property is not available for the selected dates\"). The booking is not created.\n--\n537-#### Test: Booking card is sticky on desktop viewport\n538-- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page on a desktop viewport.\n539-- **Action:** User scrolls down the page past the booking card's initial position.\n540:- **Expected:** The booking card remains visible in a sticky sidebar position as the user scrolls through the property description, amenities, and reviews.\n541-\n542-#### Test: Booking card date pickers and guest selector are functional on repeated use\n543-- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page.\n--\n547-### Component: ReviewsSection\n548-\n549-#### Test: Reviews section displays average ratings by category\n550:- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/properties/:id` for a property with multiple reviews. The average ratings are: cleanliness 4.5, accuracy 4.2, communication 4.8, location 4.6, value 4.0.\n551-- **Expected:** The reviews section shows a summary with average ratings for each category: \"Cleanliness: 4.5\", \"Accuracy: 4.2\", \"Communication: 4.8\", \"Location: 4.6\", \"Value: 4.0\". Each rating is displayed with a star icon or progress bar. An overall average rating is also displayed.\n552-\n553-#### Test: Reviews section displays overall average rating and total review count\n554:- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page with 15 reviews and an overall average rating of 4.3.\n555-- **Expected:** The reviews section header shows a star icon with \"4.3\" and \"15 reviews\" (or similar format like \"4.3 · 15 reviews\").\n556-\n557-#### Test: Reviews section displays individual review cards\n558:- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page with reviews. A review exists from guest \"Alice\" dated \"2026-01-15\" with rating 5 and comment \"Amazing place, loved every minute!\".\n559-- **Expected:** An individual review card is displayed showing the guest name \"Alice\", the date \"January 2026\" (or similar formatted date), a star rating of 5, and the comment text \"Amazing place, loved every minute!\".\n560-\n561-#### Test: Review cards display guest avatar or initial\n562:- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page with reviews. A reviewer has an avatar_url set, another reviewer does not.\n563-- **Expected:** Review cards show the guest's avatar image when available. When no avatar is set, a placeholder (e.g., first initial in a circle) is displayed.\n564-\n565-#### Test: Reviews section shows message when property has no reviews\n566:- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with no reviews.\n567-- **Expected:** The reviews section displays a message like \"No reviews yet\" instead of an empty review list. Category average ratings are not shown.\n568-\n569-#### Test: Reviews section handles pagination or \"Show more\" for many reviews\n570:- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page with more than 6 reviews.\n571-- **Expected:** An initial subset of reviews is displayed (e.g., 6 reviews). A \"Show all X reviews\" button is visible at the bottom (where X is the total count).\n572-\n573-#### Test: Clicking \"Show all reviews\" reveals all review cards\n--\n576-- **Expected:** All review cards are displayed. The button disappears or changes to \"Show less\".\n577-\n578-#### Test: Reviews are ordered by most recent first\n579:- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page with multiple reviews created on different dates.\n580-- **Expected:** Review cards are displayed in reverse chronological order, with the most recently created review appearing first.\n581-\n582-### Component: HostInfoCard\n583-\n584-#### Test: Host info card displays host name, avatar, bio, and member since date\n585:- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/properties/:id`. The property host has name \"Jane Host\", an avatar_url, bio \"Superhostess who loves sharing her properties\", and created_at \"2023-06-15\".\n586-- **Expected:** The host info card displays: the host's avatar image, name \"Jane Host\", bio text \"Superhostess who loves sharing her properties\", and \"Member since June 2023\" (formatted from created_at).\n587-\n588-#### Test: Host info card displays number of listings\n589:- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page. The host has 5 active property listings.\n590-- **Expected:** The host info card shows \"5 listings\" (or similar format like \"5 properties\").\n591-\n592-#### Test: Host info card shows placeholder avatar when host has no avatar\n593:- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page. The host has avatar_url set to null.\n594-- **Expected:** A placeholder avatar (e.g., first initial in a circle or a generic person icon) is displayed instead of a broken image.\n595-\n596-#### Test: Host info card displays correctly when host has no bio\n597:- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page. The host has bio set to null.\n598-- **Expected:** The host info card displays the host name, avatar, and member since date. The bio area is either not shown or displays a default message. No empty or broken layout.\n599-\n600-## Page: My Trips (`/trips`)\n--\n605-\n606-#### Test: My Trips page requires login\n607-- **Initial state:** User is not logged in.\n608:- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips`.\n609-- **Expected:** The user is redirected to the login page (`/login`). The My Trips page content is not displayed.\n610-\n611-#### Test: My Trips page defaults to Upcoming tab\n612:- **Initial state:** User is logged in and navigates to `/trips`.\n613-- **Expected:** The page displays three tabs: \"Upcoming\", \"Past\", and \"Cancelled\". The \"Upcoming\" tab is selected/highlighted by default. The content area shows upcoming trips (bookings with status \"pending\" or \"confirmed\" and check_in date >= today).\n614-\n615-#### Test: Upcoming tab shows pending and confirmed future bookings\n--\n666-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page. One booking has a property with images, another has a property with no images.\n667-- **Expected:** The trip card for the property with images shows the main property image. The trip card for the property without images shows a placeholder image.\n668-\n669:#### Test: Clicking trip card navigates to booking details\n670-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page. A trip card is displayed for a booking with id \"booking-123\".\n671-- **Action:** User clicks on the trip card (not the cancel or review button).\n672:- **Expected:** The app navigates to a booking detail view showing full booking information including property details, dates, guest count, price breakdown, and special requests.\n673-\n674-#### Test: Cancel button appears on pending bookings\n675-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Upcoming\" tab. A booking with status \"pending\" is displayed.\n--\n695-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Past\" tab. A completed booking exists that already has an associated review.\n696-- **Expected:** The trip card does not show a \"Write Review\" button. Instead, it may show \"Reviewed\" text or a checkmark indicating a review was already submitted.\n697-\n698:#### Test: Clicking Write Review button navigates to review page\n699-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Past\" tab. A completed booking with id \"booking-456\" has no review.\n700-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Write Review\" button on that trip card.\n701:- **Expected:** The app navigates to `/trips/booking-456/review` (the Write Review page).\n702-\n703-#### Test: Write Review button does not appear on pending, confirmed, or cancelled bookings\n704-- **Initial state:** User is logged in. Bookings exist with statuses \"pending\", \"confirmed\", and \"cancelled\".\n--\n752-\n753-#### Test: Host Dashboard requires login — redirects unauthenticated users\n754-- **Initial state:** No user is logged in.\n755:- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n756-- **Expected:** The app redirects the user to `/login`. The Host Dashboard is not rendered.\n757-\n758-#### Test: Host Dashboard requires host status — shows upgrade prompt for non-hosts\n759-- **Initial state:** A user is logged in with `is_host` set to false.\n760:- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n761:- **Expected:** The page displays a message indicating the user is not a host (e.g., \"You need to become a host to access this page\") with a link or button to navigate to their profile page (`/profile`) where they can become a host.\n762-\n763-#### Test: Stats overview displays total listings count\n764-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with 5 active properties and 1 inactive property in the database.\n765:- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n766-- **Expected:** The StatsOverview section displays a \"Total Listings\" stat card showing \"5\" (only active listings counted). The card has a label \"Total Listings\" and a numeric value.\n767-\n768-#### Test: Stats overview displays active bookings count\n769-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. Their properties have 3 bookings with status \"confirmed\", 2 with status \"pending\", and 4 with status \"completed\".\n770:- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n771-- **Expected:** The StatsOverview section displays an \"Active Bookings\" stat card showing \"5\" (pending + confirmed bookings). The card has a label \"Active Bookings\" and a numeric value.\n772-\n773-#### Test: Stats overview displays total earnings\n774-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. Their properties have completed bookings with total_price values of $500, $750, and $1200.\n775:- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n776-- **Expected:** The StatsOverview section displays a \"Total Earnings\" stat card showing \"$2,450\" (sum of completed booking total prices). The value is formatted as currency.\n777-\n778-#### Test: Stats overview displays average rating\n779-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. Their properties have reviews with overall ratings of 4, 5, 3, and 5.\n780:- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n781-- **Expected:** The StatsOverview section displays an \"Average Rating\" stat card showing \"4.3\" (average of all review ratings, rounded to one decimal). A star icon is displayed next to the value.\n782-\n783-#### Test: Stats overview shows zeros for a new host with no data\n784-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with no properties, no bookings, and no reviews.\n785:- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n786-- **Expected:** All four stat cards display zero/empty values: \"Total Listings: 0\", \"Active Bookings: 0\", \"Total Earnings: $0\", and \"Average Rating: —\" (or \"N/A\" when no reviews exist).\n787-\n788:#### Test: Host Dashboard displays navigation tabs for Listings and Bookings\n789-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host.\n790:- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n791-- **Expected:** Below the stats overview, two tabs are visible: \"Listings\" and \"Bookings\". The \"Listings\" tab is active/selected by default.\n792-\n793-#### Test: Switching between Listings and Bookings tabs\n--\n799-\n800-#### Test: Listings tab displays host's properties in a grid\n801-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with 3 active properties: \"Beach House\" ($150/night), \"Mountain Cabin\" ($200/night), \"City Loft\" ($120/night).\n802:- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting` (Listings tab is active by default).\n803-- **Expected:** A grid of 3 property cards is displayed. Each card shows the property title, main image, price per night, and status (active/inactive).\n804-\n805-#### Test: Listing card shows property details\n806-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with a property: title \"Beach House\", price $150/night, city \"Malibu\", 4.5 average rating, 10 reviews, active status.\n807-- **Expected:** The listing card displays the property title \"Beach House\", price \"$150/night\", location \"Malibu\", average rating \"4.5\" with star icon, review count \"10 reviews\", and a green \"Active\" badge.\n808-\n809:#### Test: Listing card has Edit button that navigates to property detail\n810-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with a property (id \"prop-123\").\n811-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Edit\" button on the property card.\n812:- **Expected:** The app navigates to `/properties/prop-123` where the host can view and edit their property details.\n813-\n814-#### Test: Listing card has Deactivate button for active properties\n815-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with an active property \"Beach House\".\n--\n1051-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Publish\" button.\n1052-- **Expected:** The app calls `POST /api/properties` with the property data, then `POST /api/property-images` for each photo. A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Listing published successfully!\"). The form closes. The new property appears in the Listings tab grid. The \"Total Listings\" stat increments by 1.\n1053-\n1054:#### Test: Back button navigates to the previous step\n1055-- **Initial state:** User is on Step 3 of the Add Listing form.\n1056-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Back\" button.\n1057:- **Expected:** The form navigates to Step 2. All previously entered data in Step 2 is preserved (city, address, etc. are still filled).\n1058-\n1059-#### Test: Cancel button closes the form without saving\n1060-- **Initial state:** User is on Step 4 of the Add Listing form with data entered in Steps 1–3.\n--\n1073-\n1074-#### Test: Step indicator shows correct progress throughout the form\n1075-- **Initial state:** User opens the Add Listing form.\n1076:- **Action:** User navigates through all 7 steps using Next/Back buttons.\n1077-- **Expected:** The step indicator accurately shows the current step (e.g., \"Step 1 of 7\", \"Step 2 of 7\", etc.) at each stage. Completed steps may show a checkmark or different styling.\n1078-\n1079:#### Test: Data persistence across steps when navigating back and forth\n1080-- **Initial state:** User has filled out Steps 1–5 and is on Step 5.\n1081-- **Action:** User clicks \"Back\" twice to Step 3, then \"Next\" twice to Step 5.\n1082:- **Expected:** All data entered in Steps 3, 4, and 5 is preserved after navigating back and forth. No data is lost.\n1083-\n1084-#### Test: Add Listing form works correctly on repeated use\n1085-- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. User has already published one listing successfully.\n--\n1094-\n1095-#### Test: Profile page requires login\n1096-- **Initial state:** User is not logged in.\n1097:- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n1098-- **Expected:** The user is redirected to `/login`. The profile page is not displayed.\n1099-\n1100-#### Test: Profile page displays current user info\n1101-- **Initial state:** User is logged in with name \"Alice Smith\", email \"alice@example.com\", bio \"Love traveling!\", phone \"555-1234\", avatar URL \"https://example.com/avatar.jpg\".\n1102:- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n1103-- **Expected:** The profile form displays the current values: name \"Alice Smith\", email \"alice@example.com\" (read-only), bio \"Love traveling!\", phone \"555-1234\", and avatar URL \"https://example.com/avatar.jpg\". The avatar image is displayed using the URL.\n1104-\n1105-#### Test: Edit name field inline\n--\n1142-- **Action:** User views the profile form.\n1143-- **Expected:** The email \"alice@example.com\" is displayed but the field is read-only / disabled and cannot be edited.\n1144-\n1145:#### Test: Profile update persists across navigation\n1146-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with bio \"Old bio\".\n1147:- **Action:** User changes bio to \"New bio\", clicks \"Save\", then navigates to `/` (home page), then navigates back to `/profile`.\n1148-- **Expected:** The bio field displays \"New bio\", confirming the change was persisted to the database and Redux state.\n1149-\n1150-### Component: BecomeHostButton\n1151-\n1152-#### Test: Become a Host button is visible for non-host users\n1153-- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `false`.\n1154:- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n1155-- **Expected:** A \"Become a Host\" button is visible on the profile page.\n1156-\n1157-#### Test: Become a Host button is hidden for existing hosts\n1158-- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `true`.\n1159:- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n1160-- **Expected:** The \"Become a Host\" button is NOT visible on the profile page.\n1161-\n1162-#### Test: Clicking Become a Host sets user as host\n1163-- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `false` and on `/profile`.\n1164-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Become a Host\" button.\n1165:- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog appears (e.g., \"Are you sure you want to become a host?\"). User confirms. A `POST /api/users/:id/become-host` request is sent. Upon success, the button disappears, a success message is shown (e.g., \"You are now a host!\"), and the Redux user state updates `is_host` to `true`. The \"Hosting\" link becomes available in the navigation sidebar.\n1166-\n1167-#### Test: Cancel Become a Host confirmation dialog\n1168-- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `false` and on `/profile`. The \"Become a Host\" button is visible.\n--\n1178-\n1179-#### Test: Reviews list displays user's written reviews\n1180-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has written 3 reviews for different properties (e.g., \"Cozy Cabin\" rated 5, \"City Apartment\" rated 3, \"Beach Villa\" rated 4).\n1181:- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n1182-- **Expected:** A \"My Reviews\" section is visible showing all 3 reviews. Each review card displays: the property title, the overall rating (with filled/unfilled stars), the comment text, and the date the review was written.\n1183-\n1184-#### Test: Reviews list shows empty state for user with no reviews\n1185-- **Initial state:** User is logged in but has not written any reviews.\n1186:- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n1187-- **Expected:** The \"My Reviews\" section displays an empty state message (e.g., \"You haven't written any reviews yet\") instead of review cards.\n1188-\n1189-#### Test: Review card shows rating with star display\n1190-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has written a review with overall rating 4 out of 5.\n1191:- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n1192-- **Expected:** The review card displays 4 filled stars and 1 unfilled star, matching the rating value.\n1193-\n1194-#### Test: Review card links to the reviewed property\n1195-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has written a review for property \"Cozy Cabin\" (property ID \"abc-123\").\n1196-- **Action:** User clicks on the property title \"Cozy Cabin\" in a review card.\n1197:- **Expected:** The user is navigated to `/properties/abc-123` (the property detail page for \"Cozy Cabin\").\n1198-\n1199-#### Test: Reviews list shows review details correctly\n1200-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has written a review with rating 5, comment \"Amazing stay! The host was very welcoming.\", for property \"Beach Villa\", dated \"2026-01-15\".\n1201:- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n1202-- **Expected:** The review card displays: property title \"Beach Villa\", 5 filled stars, comment text \"Amazing stay! The host was very welcoming.\", and date \"Jan 15, 2026\".\n1203-\n1204-#### Test: Reviews list updates after writing a new review\n1205-- **Initial state:** User is logged in, on `/profile`, and has 2 existing reviews displayed.\n1206:- **Action:** User navigates to a completed booking, writes a new review, submits it, then navigates back to `/profile`.\n1207-- **Expected:** The \"My Reviews\" section now displays 3 reviews, including the newly written review with the correct property title, rating, and comment.\n1208-\n1209-#### Test: Reviews list shows multiple reviews in chronological order\n1210-- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has written reviews on different dates: \"Beach Villa\" on 2026-01-15, \"City Apartment\" on 2026-02-10, \"Cozy Cabin\" on 2026-03-05.\n1211:- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n1212-- **Expected:** The reviews are displayed in reverse chronological order (newest first): \"Cozy Cabin\" (Mar 5, 2026), \"City Apartment\" (Feb 10, 2026), \"Beach Villa\" (Jan 15, 2026).\n1213-\n1214-## Page: Write Review (`/trips/:bookingId/review`)\n--\n1219-\n1220-#### Test: Property info displays for the booking being reviewed\n1221-- **Initial state:** User \"guest@example.com\" is logged in and has a completed booking (booking-789) for \"Oceanfront Villa\" in Malibu, CA with check-in 2026-01-10 and check-out 2026-01-15.\n1222:- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review`.\n1223-- **Expected:** The page displays the property context section showing the property title \"Oceanfront Villa\", the location \"Malibu, CA\", the property's main image, check-in date \"Jan 10, 2026\", check-out date \"Jan 15, 2026\", and the number of nights (5 nights).\n1224-\n1225-#### Test: Property booking context shows guest count\n1226-- **Initial state:** User is logged in with a completed booking (booking-789) for 3 guests at \"Oceanfront Villa\".\n1227:- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review`.\n1228-- **Expected:** The property booking context section displays \"3 guests\" alongside the booking dates.\n1229-\n1230-#### Test: Property booking context shows total price paid\n1231-- **Initial state:** User is logged in with a completed booking (booking-789) with a total_price of $1,250.\n1232:- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review`.\n1233-- **Expected:** The property booking context displays the total price \"$1,250\" that was paid for the booking.\n1234-\n1235-#### Test: Redirect to login if not authenticated\n1236-- **Initial state:** No user is logged in.\n1237:- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review`.\n1238-- **Expected:** The app redirects the user to `/login`. The Write Review page is not displayed.\n1239-\n1240-#### Test: Error state when booking does not exist\n1241-- **Initial state:** User \"guest@example.com\" is logged in.\n1242:- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/nonexistent-booking-id/review`.\n1243-- **Expected:** The page displays an error message such as \"Booking not found\" and does not show the review form.\n1244-\n1245-#### Test: Error state when booking belongs to another user\n1246-- **Initial state:** User \"other@example.com\" is logged in. Booking booking-789 belongs to \"guest@example.com\".\n1247:- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review`.\n1248-- **Expected:** The page displays an error message such as \"You cannot review this booking\" and does not show the review form.\n1249-\n1250-#### Test: Error state when booking is not completed\n1251-- **Initial state:** User \"guest@example.com\" is logged in with a booking (booking-pending) that has status \"pending\".\n1252:- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-pending/review`.\n1253-- **Expected:** The page displays an error message such as \"You can only review completed bookings\" and does not show the review form.\n1254-\n1255-#### Test: Error state when review already exists for booking\n1256-- **Initial state:** User \"guest@example.com\" is logged in with a completed booking (booking-reviewed) that already has a review submitted.\n1257:- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-reviewed/review`.\n1258-- **Expected:** The page displays a message such as \"You have already reviewed this booking\" and does not show the review form. Optionally shows a link back to My Trips.\n1259-\n1260-### Component: RatingSliders\n1261-\n1262-#### Test: All six rating sliders display with default values\n1263:- **Initial state:** User is logged in and navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review` for a completed booking.\n1264-- **Expected:** Six rating sliders are visible with labels: \"Overall\", \"Cleanliness\", \"Accuracy\", \"Communication\", \"Location\", and \"Value\". Each slider defaults to a mid-range value (e.g., 3 out of 5) or is unset, and shows the current numeric value.\n1265-\n1266-#### Test: Adjust overall rating slider\n--\n1311-### Component: ReviewForm\n1312-\n1313-#### Test: Review form displays comment text area\n1314:- **Initial state:** User is logged in and navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review` for a completed booking.\n1315-- **Expected:** A text area is visible with a placeholder such as \"Write your review...\" or \"Tell others about your experience\" for entering the review comment.\n1316-\n1317-#### Test: Submit button is visible\n--\n1326-#### Test: Submit review with all ratings and comment\n1327-- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page. User has set Overall to 5, Cleanliness to 5, Accuracy to 4, Communication to 5, Location to 4, Value to 4, and typed \"Wonderful experience, would definitely come back!\" in the comment area.\n1328-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Submit Review\" button.\n1329:- **Expected:** The review is submitted successfully via `POST /api/reviews`. The app navigates back to `/trips` (My Trips page). A success notification or message such as \"Review submitted successfully\" appears.\n1330-\n1331-#### Test: Submitted review appears on property detail page\n1332-- **Initial state:** User just submitted a review for booking-789 (property \"Oceanfront Villa\") with Overall rating 5 and comment \"Wonderful experience, would definitely come back!\".\n1333:- **Action:** User navigates to the property detail page for \"Oceanfront Villa\" (`/properties/:id`).\n1334-- **Expected:** The reviews section shows the newly submitted review with the guest's name, the rating of 5, and the comment \"Wonderful experience, would definitely come back!\". The property's average rating and review count are updated.\n1335-\n1336-#### Test: Submitted review appears in user profile reviews list\n1337-- **Initial state:** User just submitted a review for \"Oceanfront Villa\".\n1338:- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n1339-- **Expected:** The user's reviews list includes the newly submitted review for \"Oceanfront Villa\" with the correct rating and comment.\n1340-\n1341-#### Test: Submit review with ratings but no comment\n1342-- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page. User has set all six rating sliders (Overall: 3, Cleanliness: 3, Accuracy: 3, Communication: 3, Location: 3, Value: 3) but left the comment text area empty.\n1343-- **Action:** User clicks the \"Submit Review\" button.\n1344:- **Expected:** The review is submitted successfully (comment is optional per the data model). The app navigates back to `/trips`.\n1345-\n1346-#### Test: Submit button is disabled when ratings are not set\n1347:- **Initial state:** User navigates to the Write Review page. No rating sliders have been adjusted from their unset/default state.\n1348-- **Expected:** The \"Submit Review\" button is disabled or grayed out, preventing submission without ratings.\n1349-\n1350-#### Test: Form validation prevents submission without all ratings\n--\n1357-- **Action:** User clicks \"Write Review\", fills out all ratings (all set to 4) and a comment \"Great stay!\", and clicks \"Submit Review\". User is redirected to `/trips`.\n1358-- **Expected:** The trip card for \"Oceanfront Villa\" no longer shows the \"Write Review\" button. It may show \"Reviewed\" text or a checkmark instead.\n1359-\n1360:#### Test: Navigate back from review page without submitting\n1361-- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page and has set some ratings and typed partial comment text.\n1362:- **Action:** User clicks the browser back button or a \"Cancel\" / back navigation link on the page.\n1363-- **Expected:** The user is taken back to `/trips`. No review is submitted. The \"Write Review\" button still appears on the trip card.\n1364-\n1365-#### Test: Comment text area allows multi-line input\n--\n1369-\n1370-#### Test: Re-visiting review page after submission shows already-reviewed state\n1371-- **Initial state:** User \"guest@example.com\" has already submitted a review for booking-789.\n1372:- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review` directly via URL.\n1373-- **Expected:** The page displays a message such as \"You have already reviewed this booking\" instead of the review form. A link to return to My Trips is available.","numLines":554}}
