[2026-03-14T19:52:29.237Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HionivL3TUDxaVYmmkm2i1","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→7-### Component: AuthToggle\n     2→8-\n     3→9-#### Test: Auth page defaults to login mode\n     4→10:- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/login` for the first time (not logged in).\n     5→11-- **Expected:** The page displays in login mode with the email input field visible, a \"Log In\" submit button, and a toggle link reading \"Don't have an account? Register\" at the bottom.\n     6→12-\n     7→13-#### Test: Toggle from login to register mode\n     8→--\n     9→91-### Component: SearchBar\n    10→92-\n    11→93-#### Test: Search bar displays all input fields on load\n    12→94:- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page (`/`).\n    13→95-- **Expected:** The search bar is visible at the top of the page containing four inputs: a location text input with placeholder \"Where are you going?\", a check-in date picker, a check-out date picker, and a guest count selector. A search/submit button with a magnifying glass icon is visible.\n    14→96-\n    15→97-#### Test: Search by location filters property results\n    16→--\n    17→142-### Component: CategoryFilter\n    18→143-\n    19→144-#### Test: Category filter bar displays all property type chips\n    20→145:- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page (`/`).\n    21→146-- **Expected:** A horizontal scrollable bar of category chips is displayed below the search bar. Chips are shown for each property type: \"Apartment\", \"House\", \"Cabin\", \"Villa\", \"Condo\", \"Loft\", \"Cottage\", \"Townhouse\". No chip is selected by default (all properties are shown).\n    22→147-\n    23→148-#### Test: Clicking a category chip filters properties by that type\n    24→--\n    25→177-### Component: PropertyGrid\n    26→178-\n    27→179-#### Test: Property grid displays properties in a responsive grid layout\n    28→180:- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page. Multiple properties exist in the database.\n    29→181-- **Expected:** Properties are displayed in a responsive grid: 1 column on mobile, 2 columns on tablet, 3-4 columns on desktop. Each property is rendered as a PropertyCard.\n    30→182-\n    31→183-#### Test: Property grid shows message when no properties match filters\n    32→--\n    33→186-- **Expected:** The property grid area displays a \"No properties found\" message instead of an empty grid. The message suggests adjusting filters or search criteria.\n    34→187-\n    35→188-#### Test: Property grid loads and displays properties from API on initial page load\n    36→189:- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page. Properties exist in the database.\n    37→190-- **Expected:** The grid fetches properties via `GET /api/properties` and displays property cards. While loading, a loading indicator is shown. Once loaded, the property cards appear with correct data.\n    38→191-\n    39→192-### Component: PropertyCard\n    40→--\n    41→199-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. A property exists with at least one image (the first image by display_order).\n    42→200-- **Expected:** The property card displays the main image (lowest display_order) at the top of the card with rounded top corners. If no image exists, a placeholder image is shown.\n    43→201-\n    44→202:#### Test: Clicking a property card navigates to property detail page\n    45→203-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. A property with id \"abc-123\" is displayed.\n    46→204-- **Action:** User clicks on the property card (not the favorite button).\n    47→205:- **Expected:** The app navigates to `/properties/abc-123` (the property detail page).\n    48→206-\n    49→207-#### Test: Property card displays property type badge\n    50→208-- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties of different types exist."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f7a7c36-f6a4-4f04-ab3c-97ac5928ffe